  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25146664",
      "title": "Getting User Input & Handling Form Submission",
      "lectureOrder": 73,
      "videoOrder": 68,
      "sourceHash": "027b6509f8e53f4ea44ffbc44aea21b315123ff6ab3353ce74e7971173cd66ee",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.24,
          "end": 4.01,
          "en": "Now to handle the form submission,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.01,
          "end": 6.82,
          "en": "we got to do two main things,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.82,
          "end": 9.78,
          "en": "we have to listen to the form submission.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.78,
          "end": 13.4,
          "en": "And we then actually have to prevent the browser default,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.4,
          "end": 17.17,
          "en": "which is that it sends an HTTP request automatically,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.17,
          "end": 19.21,
          "en": "and hence it would reload the page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.21,
          "end": 22.95,
          "en": "We wanna prevent this and instead handle the submission",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.95,
          "end": 26.17,
          "en": "with JavaScript with react.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.17,
          "end": 28.12,
          "en": "And in addition to that, we of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.12,
          "end": 30.8,
          "en": "need to read the entered values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.8,
          "end": 34.193,
          "en": "we need to get the actual input the user entered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 35.3,
          "end": 37.89,
          "en": "Let's start with the form submission.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 37.89,
          "end": 39.38,
          "en": "To listen for that submission,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 39.38,
          "end": 42.73,
          "en": "we can add the on submit prop on the form,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 42.73,
          "end": 46.45,
          "en": "because by default, a submit event will be emitted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 46.45,
          "end": 49.73,
          "en": "if you have a button in a form and that button is clicked.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 49.73,
          "end": 52.23,
          "en": "And we can then catch this submit event here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 52.23,
          "end": 56.96,
          "en": "and run our own logic with help of that on submit prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 56.96,
          "end": 59.2,
          "en": "Now I will add another nested function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 59.2,
          "end": 62.01,
          "en": "in the new meetup forum component function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 62.01,
          "end": 65.93,
          "en": "let's say the submit handler, which should be triggered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 65.93,
          "end": 70.25,
          "en": "when the submit event occurs by connecting function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 70.25,
          "end": 72.133,
          "en": "and on submit like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 73.3,
          "end": 75.53999999999999,
          "en": "But as I mentioned, a couple of seconds ago,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 75.53999999999999,
          "end": 79.51,
          "en": "the default behavior of the browser would actually be",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 79.51,
          "end": 80.96000000000001,
          "en": "that it sends a request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 80.96000000000001,
          "end": 84.87,
          "en": "to the server serving this page automatically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 84.87,
          "end": 88.46000000000001,
          "en": "And we don't want that we don't want that browser default.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 88.46000000000001,
          "end": 91.17,
          "en": "Instead, we wanna prevent that default,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 91.17,
          "end": 94.36,
          "en": "and run our own JavaScript logic.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 94.36,
          "end": 96.37,
          "en": "That might and still involve",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 96.37,
          "end": 98.94,
          "en": "that we send that HTTP request later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 98.94,
          "end": 102.62,
          "en": "But we wanna send that request behind the scenes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 102.62,
          "end": 104.75999999999999,
          "en": "without reloading the page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 104.75999999999999,
          "end": 106.33,
          "en": "which is what would happen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 106.33,
          "end": 109.16,
          "en": "if the browser does its default thing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 109.16,
          "end": 113.65,
          "en": "Now, thankfully, preventing that browser default is simple.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 113.65,
          "end": 117.65,
          "en": "We will get an event object automatically here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 117.65,
          "end": 121.42,
          "en": "Because all those built in events like on click, on submit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 121.42,
          "end": 124.17,
          "en": "and all the other events to which we can listen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 124.17,
          "end": 125.61,
          "en": "for all those events,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 125.61,
          "end": 129.53,
          "en": "react will automatically pass an event argument",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 129.53,
          "end": 133.35,
          "en": "into the function that is executed for those events.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 133.35,
          "end": 136.89,
          "en": "This argument which we can accept here as a parameter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 136.89,
          "end": 141.89,
          "en": "and this event object will have a prevent default method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 142.4,
          "end": 145.873,
          "en": "which we can call to prevent the browser default.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 146.74,
          "end": 149.39,
          "en": "That's actually not even react specific,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 149.39,
          "end": 151.81,
          "en": "this event object and this method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 151.81,
          "end": 154.13,
          "en": "that is a Vanilla JavaScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 154.13,
          "end": 156.773,
          "en": "which is fully supported by react.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 157.87,
          "end": 160.55,
          "en": "So that will prevent that browser default,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 160.55,
          "end": 163.97,
          "en": "and will allow us to fully handle the submission",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 163.97,
          "end": 166.833,
          "en": "with just JavaScript and react.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 168.07999999999998,
          "end": 169.96,
          "en": "So that's step one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 169.96,
          "end": 174.453,
          "en": "Now we need to find a way of reading those entered values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 175.29,
          "end": 178.04,
          "en": "For reading the entered values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 178.04,
          "end": 181.38,
          "en": "we got two main ways of handling this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 181.38,
          "end": 185.07,
          "en": "we can use use state again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 185.07,
          "end": 190.07,
          "en": "and add the on change event listener to all those inputs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 190.29,
          "end": 192.33,
          "en": "which will in the end trigger a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 192.33,
          "end": 197.32999999999998,
          "en": "for every keystroke, and then we can extract that value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 197.34,
          "end": 199.56,
          "en": "the user entered from the event object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 199.56,
          "end": 201.52,
          "en": "which will receive for that event,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 201.52,
          "end": 204.26,
          "en": "and update our state for that given input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 204.26,
          "end": 206.47,
          "en": "with the entered value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 206.47,
          "end": 208.17000000000002,
          "en": "That would allow us to keep track",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 208.17000000000002,
          "end": 211.9,
          "en": "of what the user entered with every keystroke.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 211.9,
          "end": 215.8,
          "en": "But here I'm actually only interested in the user input once",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 215.8,
          "end": 217.65,
          "en": "when the form is submitted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 217.65,
          "end": 218.483,
          "en": "And for this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 218.483,
          "end": 221.16,
          "en": "we can use a number a concept built into react,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 221.16,
          "end": 223.39,
          "en": "the concept of refs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 223.39,
          "end": 225.88,
          "en": "Now ref stands for reference.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 225.88,
          "end": 227.77,
          "en": "And react simply allows us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 227.77,
          "end": 232.22,
          "en": "to set up references cue DOM elements,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 232.22,
          "end": 236.64,
          "en": "so we can get direct access to DOM elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 236.64,
          "end": 240.04,
          "en": "To set up such a reference such a connection,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 240.04,
          "end": 245.04,
          "en": "we first of all have to import the use ref hook from react.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 245.45,
          "end": 247.26,
          "en": "So just like use state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 247.26,
          "end": 251.59,
          "en": "that's another built in special function offered by react",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 251.59,
          "end": 256.04,
          "en": "which we can execute in our functional components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 256.04,
          "end": 258.81,
          "en": "And we can execute use ref here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 258.81,
          "end": 263.697,
          "en": "And with that, we create a ref object, a reference object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 263.697,
          "end": 267.34,
          "en": "and we can store this in a constant and we could name it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 267.34,
          "end": 271.61,
          "en": "title input ref, because my first ref here should be",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 271.61,
          "end": 273.443,
          "en": "for this title input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 274.44,
          "end": 277.71,
          "en": "Now to connect this created object to this input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 277.71,
          "end": 281.78,
          "en": "we add another special prop to this HTML element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 281.78,
          "end": 285.22,
          "en": "And now very special prop besides the key prop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 285.22,
          "end": 286.8,
          "en": "which is built into react",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 286.8,
          "end": 291.07,
          "en": "and supported on all elements out of the box,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 291.07,
          "end": 293.89,
          "en": "and that's the ref prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 293.89,
          "end": 296.8,
          "en": "We add the ref prop to this input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 296.8,
          "end": 300.663,
          "en": "and as a value, we point at this title input ref,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 301.55,
          "end": 305.09,
          "en": "this will establish a connection and will give us access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 305.09,
          "end": 308.573,
          "en": "to this input element through this ref object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 309.59,
          "end": 312.29,
          "en": "So here in this submit handler,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 312.29,
          "end": 315.14,
          "en": "we can then get the entered title.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 315.14,
          "end": 318.32,
          "en": "So the concrete value the user entered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 318.32,
          "end": 320.693,
          "en": "by using that title input ref.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 321.64,
          "end": 324.51,
          "en": "And then they're actually dot current,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 324.51,
          "end": 329.01,
          "en": "all those ref objects created with the use ref, were x such",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 329.01,
          "end": 331.03,
          "en": "that they have a current property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 331.03,
          "end": 334.53,
          "en": "which then holds the actual connected value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 334.53,
          "end": 335.87,
          "en": "And therefore it's not current,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 335.87,
          "end": 338.53,
          "en": "which then holds this input element object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 338.53,
          "end": 342.78,
          "en": "the JavaScript representation of that input element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 342.78,
          "end": 347.25,
          "en": "And all those input elements have a value property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 347.25,
          "end": 349.51,
          "en": "That's just how JavaScript works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 349.51,
          "end": 353.47,
          "en": "The JavaScript object representing an input element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 353.47,
          "end": 355.43,
          "en": "has a value property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 355.43,
          "end": 360.02,
          "en": "And that value property holds the currently entered value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 360.02,
          "end": 362.87,
          "en": "of that input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 362.87,
          "end": 365.713,
          "en": "So that's how we can extract what the user entered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 366.79,
          "end": 369.35,
          "en": "We could also change it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 369.35,
          "end": 373.7,
          "en": "we could set value to some new value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 373.7,
          "end": 376.27,
          "en": "But we shouldn't really do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 376.27,
          "end": 378.82,
          "en": "If you wanna change what's output on the screen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 378.82,
          "end": 381.48,
          "en": "use state for data and stat.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 381.48,
          "end": 385.54,
          "en": "But for reading input, for reading values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 385.54,
          "end": 388.34,
          "en": "refs can be a very useful tool.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 388.34,
          "end": 391.823,
          "en": "And here we are reading what the user entered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 393.28,
          "end": 396.37,
          "en": "Now, we can repeat that for the other inputs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 396.37,
          "end": 398.39,
          "en": "simply by creating more reps,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 398.39,
          "end": 402.27,
          "en": "you can have more than one ref per component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 402.27,
          "end": 407.27,
          "en": "So here, I also create the image, input ref, like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 410.43,
          "end": 414.37,
          "en": "and I'll already copy that a couple of times,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 414.37,
          "end": 417.71,
          "en": "and also create the address input ref",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 417.71,
          "end": 422.07,
          "en": "and the description, input ref.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 422.07,
          "end": 426.34,
          "en": "And then we connect those refs with the ref property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 426.34,
          "end": 430.38,
          "en": "Here on the image, we connect this to image input ref.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 430.38,
          "end": 434.3,
          "en": "For the address, we connect us to address input ref.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 434.3,
          "end": 438.4,
          "en": "And on the text area, which is there to enter a description,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 438.4,
          "end": 440.883,
          "en": "we connect the description input ref.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
